WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:02.542
Clones, crocodiles,
conspiracies:

00:00:02.625 --> 00:00:04.583
Resident Evil has them all.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:05.750
And unpicking
all those mysteries

00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:07.333
may require some help.

00:00:07.417 --> 00:00:08.833
We're here
to fill in the gaps

00:00:08.917 --> 00:00:11.708
and explain the implications
of hidden details,

00:00:11.792 --> 00:00:12.917
as we answer
the biggest questions

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.667
raised by the show's ending.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:16.958
We're about to inject
a whole dose of spoilers

00:00:17.042 --> 00:00:18.583
straight into your veins,

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:21.000
so make sure you've
watched Resident Evil first.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:26.875
At the end of the series,

00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:29.208
we see Jade and Billie
fleeing New Raccoon City

00:00:29.292 --> 00:00:30.708
in 2022,

00:00:30.792 --> 00:00:33.083
and an older Billie
kidnapping Jade's daughter

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:34.417
in 2036.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.417
The trickiest part
of Resident Evil

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.333
is juggling
those two timelines,

00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:40.500
with Jade and Billie
pre-apocalypse adventures

00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:41.667
in 2022,

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.250
and Jade fighting
for her life,

00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:44.500
14 years later.

00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:47.333
What we don't see
in the 2022 flashbacks

00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:49.833
is how 2036
went to the dogs,

00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:51.125
zombified or otherwise,

00:00:51.208 --> 00:00:53.125
and why Billie
turned on Jade.

00:00:53.208 --> 00:00:54.167
But throughout the show,

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.417
we're given hints
to fill in some gaps.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.167
When 2036 Jade
is caught in episode one,

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.208
the bounty hunters spot
her identity number

00:01:01.292 --> 00:01:02.458
from New Raccoon City…

00:01:02.542 --> 00:01:03.458
She's a survivor.

00:01:03.542 --> 00:01:06.292
…and confirm this is where
the zombie outbreak began.

00:01:06.375 --> 00:01:07.750
Your ink.

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:09.875
You were in the New Raccoon
when the outbreak started.

00:01:09.958 --> 00:01:12.667
As to why Billie
shoots Jade in 2036,

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.625
we do see some conflict
between the sisters in 2022,

00:01:16.708 --> 00:01:18.792
but the real indicator
hides in Billie's speech.

00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:20.833
She mentions events
that have yet

00:01:20.917 --> 00:01:22.375
to happen in the show.

00:01:22.458 --> 00:01:24.958
You ever notice how everyone
around you somehow…

00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:27.333
dies?

00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:29.625
Simon.

00:01:29.708 --> 00:01:30.917
Bert.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.333
Kim, Hiroki… Dad.

00:01:35.417 --> 00:01:37.542
Their dad blew up
destroying Umbrella's lab,

00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:38.917
and Simon is killed
by his mum

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.083
after being bitten
by Billie.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.583
#World'sWorstMother.

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:45.417
But in the 2022 timeline,
Bert is still alive

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.958
and drives off
with the girls.

00:01:47.042 --> 00:01:48.208
And we've yet
to meet characters

00:01:48.292 --> 00:01:49.458
called Kim and Hiroki -

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.417
a clear sign
that the sisters' journey

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.250
from strained siblings
to sworn enemies

00:01:53.333 --> 00:01:56.042
has plenty of secrets
yet to be revealed.

00:01:56.125 --> 00:01:57.708
Stay the fuck away from her.

00:02:00.083 --> 00:02:02.250
At the end of the season,
we see something gnarly

00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:04.542
doing his best
Carrie impersonation.

00:02:06.375 --> 00:02:08.375
The claw belongs
to this nasty-looking chap,

00:02:08.458 --> 00:02:10.542
previously contained
in Umbrella's laboratory,

00:02:10.625 --> 00:02:12.292
until Albert blows it up.

00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:13.708
And while we don't see
what triggers

00:02:13.792 --> 00:02:15.667
the zombie outbreak in 2022,

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.708
we'd bet a yearly supply
of Joy pills

00:02:17.792 --> 00:02:20.167
on it having something to do
with this guy.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.500
To understand why,

00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:23.625
we need to quickly talk
about the T-Virus.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.958
It's mentioned at several
points in the show,

00:02:28.042 --> 00:02:29.042
and has a long history

00:02:29.125 --> 00:02:31.083
in the wider
Resident Evil universe.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:34.125
But the drug contains
a derivative of the T-Virus,

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.583
a pathogen
we originally developed

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:38.542
for the American military.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:42.208
That project was… ill-fated.

00:02:42.292 --> 00:02:44.542
The T-Virus
was a mutagenic plague

00:02:44.625 --> 00:02:47.625
engineered by the Umbrella
Corporation in the 1970s.

00:02:47.708 --> 00:02:50.208
This isn't a pharmaceutical
company we see in the show,

00:02:50.292 --> 00:02:52.625
but a gang of mad scientists
mutating people

00:02:52.708 --> 00:02:55.042
into monsters
for military purposes.

00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:56.542
They create the T-Virus,

00:02:56.625 --> 00:02:59.333
and the Resident Evil games,
all set before the show,

00:02:59.417 --> 00:03:01.083
are about heroes
fighting the creatures

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:02.708
that escape as a result.

00:03:02.792 --> 00:03:05.708
Evelyn Marcus does
hint at this dark past.

00:03:05.792 --> 00:03:10.042
The old Umbrella, my father
made his share of mistakes,

00:03:10.125 --> 00:03:12.000
but this is not
that company.

00:03:12.083 --> 00:03:13.042
And she would know.

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.042
In the games,

00:03:14.125 --> 00:03:16.750
there is a character called
James Marcus, her dad.

00:03:16.833 --> 00:03:20.125
In the 2022 timeline,
the T-Virus still exists,

00:03:20.208 --> 00:03:22.542
albeit as a strain
in Umbrella's Joy pills.

00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:25.000
And this explains the weird
and wonderful creatures

00:03:25.083 --> 00:03:26.792
seen throughout the show.

00:03:26.875 --> 00:03:27.833
T-Virus does
different things

00:03:27.917 --> 00:03:29.417
to different subjects.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.958
People mostly
become zombies,

00:03:31.042 --> 00:03:33.042
but it can also mutate them
into Lickers,

00:03:33.125 --> 00:03:34.667
the guys
with the horrible tongues

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:36.250
living in
the Channel Tunnel.

00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:37.833
Wouldn't happen
on the Eurostar.

00:03:39.833 --> 00:03:41.292
If the virus gets
into animals,

00:03:41.375 --> 00:03:42.958
it increases their size,

00:03:43.042 --> 00:03:44.667
explaining
the giant spiders,

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:45.958
Jade's caterpillar friend,

00:03:46.042 --> 00:03:48.875
and the scariest crocodile
this side of Peter Pan.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.000
As for our friend
in the rubble,

00:03:52.083 --> 00:03:53.583
he resembles
the ultimate form

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.292
the virus takes
in the games:

00:03:55.375 --> 00:03:56.625
the tyrant,

00:03:56.708 --> 00:03:59.250
an unstoppable killing
machine with massive claws.

00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:01.125
Which is why releasing him
from his tank

00:04:01.208 --> 00:04:02.833
is likely to be
very bad news

00:04:02.917 --> 00:04:05.083
for the people in 2022.

00:04:07.458 --> 00:04:09.625
We learn in the series
that Jade and Billie's dad,

00:04:09.708 --> 00:04:12.833
Albert Wesker, is not
Father of the Year material.

00:04:12.917 --> 00:04:15.292
He is, in fact, a clone
of another Albert Wesker.

00:04:15.375 --> 00:04:17.000
Let's call him "OG" Wesker,

00:04:17.083 --> 00:04:19.625
a former Umbrella scientist
who made copies of himself

00:04:19.708 --> 00:04:21.500
to work on secret
science projects.

00:04:22.125 --> 00:04:23.667
We meet three clones
in the show:

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.500
Albert, Bert and Alby.

00:04:25.583 --> 00:04:27.292
Alby dies
when Umbrella soldiers

00:04:27.375 --> 00:04:28.708
storm OG Wesker's lab…

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:30.667
…leaving Bert,

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.417
who was the unhinged
breadstick-loving clone…

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.208
More breadsticks.

00:04:33.292 --> 00:04:36.167
…and Albert,
father to Jade and Billie.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.375
We learn that this Albert

00:04:37.458 --> 00:04:38.667
genetically modified
his daughters

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.208
so that their blood
could keep him alive.

00:04:40.292 --> 00:04:43.208
As a clone, his body
wasn't built to endure.

00:04:43.292 --> 00:04:45.833
At the end of the season,
Albert sacrifices himself

00:04:45.917 --> 00:04:48.333
and leaves the teens
to escape with Bert.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:52.458
The use of clones
also explains

00:04:52.542 --> 00:04:55.167
how Albert Wesker,
or a version of him,

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.125
is alive in 2022.

00:04:57.208 --> 00:04:59.667
In the Resident Evil
universe, OG Wesker,

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.000
the mastermind with the cool
glasses and leather coat,

00:05:02.083 --> 00:05:03.792
fell into some lava
in 2009 -

00:05:05.042 --> 00:05:06.708
a fact the show
does reference.

00:05:06.792 --> 00:05:09.042
He was killed by
the original Albert Wesker,

00:05:09.125 --> 00:05:10.042
our creator.

00:05:10.125 --> 00:05:11.333
Creator?

00:05:11.417 --> 00:05:13.417
We were part of a research
and development team

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.375
he put together to help him.

00:05:15.458 --> 00:05:16.542
He died in a volcano.

00:05:16.625 --> 00:05:18.042
It's okay though.
He wasn't very nice.

00:05:18.125 --> 00:05:19.917
Yeah, it was a whole thing.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.250
If you're familiar
with the wider

00:05:21.333 --> 00:05:22.458
Resident Evil universe,

00:05:22.542 --> 00:05:25.042
it does explain a few
moments in the season.

00:05:25.125 --> 00:05:27.875
We see OG Wesker
in a flashback to 2005,

00:05:27.958 --> 00:05:30.375
set in a place called
the Arklay Mountains.

00:05:30.458 --> 00:05:32.125
This is the location
of the very first

00:05:32.208 --> 00:05:33.167
Resident Evil game,

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:35.125
where Umbrella
made the T-Virus.

00:05:35.208 --> 00:05:37.083
It's also OG Wesker
we see and hear

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:39.625
in a tape the sisters find
in their dad's hidden room.

00:05:39.708 --> 00:05:40.792
The video shows Wesker

00:05:40.875 --> 00:05:43.417
injecting a mutated woman
named Lisa.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.583
Again, she's a character
from the first game,

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:46.583
Lisa Trevor,

00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:49.083
who appears in this
horrific, monstrous form.

00:05:51.167 --> 00:05:53.000
Oh, and if you're wondering
where dad Albert

00:05:53.083 --> 00:05:55.083
gets his weird approach
to home security,

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:57.625
the tune the girls play on
the piano to unlock his room

00:05:57.708 --> 00:05:59.458
is Beethoven's
"Moonlight Sonata",

00:05:59.542 --> 00:06:00.667
which you played on a piano

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.667
in the original
Resident Evil game

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:04.417
to unlock
a different secret room.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.542
In fact,
the whole fifth episode,

00:06:06.625 --> 00:06:07.542
"Family Movies",

00:06:07.625 --> 00:06:09.667
feels like a love letter
to Resident Evil puzzles.

00:06:10.292 --> 00:06:11.583
Blowing a dog whistle
to grab a key

00:06:11.667 --> 00:06:12.583
from a dog's collar

00:06:12.667 --> 00:06:14.250
is another conundrum
from the game.

00:06:14.333 --> 00:06:16.417
You chipped fuzzy baby.

00:06:18.792 --> 00:06:20.708
One final mystery
from the ending:

00:06:20.792 --> 00:06:22.333
before his explosive
resignation,

00:06:22.417 --> 00:06:25.375
Albert writes the name of
a helpful contact on a note.

00:06:25.458 --> 00:06:27.667
In the final shots
of the show,

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:29.542
this is revealed
to read "Ada Wong".

00:06:29.625 --> 00:06:30.625
Like OG Wesker,

00:06:30.708 --> 00:06:32.042
she's another key character

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:33.708
in the Resident Evil
universe,

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:35.542
a spy whose
shifting alliances

00:06:35.625 --> 00:06:37.250
could never be pinned down.

00:06:37.333 --> 00:06:38.958
That she works
outside of Umbrella,

00:06:39.042 --> 00:06:41.167
or at least did
in her video-game past,

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:43.583
would suggest she's a wise
person to turn to,

00:06:43.667 --> 00:06:45.542
given
their current situation.

00:06:45.625 --> 00:06:48.375
In the wider universe,
Ada first appeared in 1998

00:06:48.458 --> 00:06:49.750
during a zombie outbreak

00:06:49.833 --> 00:06:51.667
in the original
Raccoon City.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.000
This is the event referenced
throughout the show.

00:06:54.083 --> 00:06:55.333
The girls find
reference to it

00:06:55.417 --> 00:06:57.250
in their dad's 1998 files,

00:06:57.333 --> 00:06:59.625
and they learn that things
didn't end well there.

00:06:59.708 --> 00:07:02.208
Do you know what happened
to the first Racoon City?

00:07:02.917 --> 00:07:05.250
Some kind of gas leak,
a big fire or something.

00:07:05.333 --> 00:07:08.000
No, no, no, it was destroyed
by a nuclear blast.

00:07:08.083 --> 00:07:10.625
But hey, if Ada survived
one zombie apocalypse,

00:07:10.708 --> 00:07:11.958
maybe she can
survive another.

00:07:12.583 --> 00:07:15.375
Intriguingly, her address
is listed as Tokyo.

00:07:15.458 --> 00:07:17.917
Does this hint at more
globetrotting to come?

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.417
A trip to Japan
would explain

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.333
how Jade and Billie
could meet a Hiroko,

00:07:21.417 --> 00:07:23.167
one of the mystery
characters Billie says

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:26.833
Jade has killed
between 2022 and 2036.

00:07:26.917 --> 00:07:28.708
Only time will tell.

00:07:28.792 --> 00:07:31.250
And so we've reached
the end of Resident Evil,

00:07:31.333 --> 00:07:32.875
a world with
as many brainteasers

00:07:32.958 --> 00:07:34.458
as it has brain-munchers.

00:07:34.542 --> 00:07:36.500
Why not share your own
theories in the comments?

00:07:36.583 --> 00:07:38.167
And if you enjoyed
this breakdown,

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:40.333
subscribe to
Still Watching Netflix

00:07:40.417 --> 00:07:42.042
for more videos like it.

